From b17b168d2d66d58a9b3011c8b0b44a70eaf680af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:04:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sinker): read a welded wall face as its vertical strips

A rounded-corner pocket's wall band welds into one smooth face
(FeatureSel::Patch). The electrode-from-faces read refused that pick
as "a curved wall". Now the app expands the patch into its planar
strips, and the new motion rule sinker_cavity::welded_wall holds each
strip to the vertical-wall rule. The cavity read then stands each strip
on the floor ring like any wall. The floor and the welded face give the
same body electrode as the planar-strip pick (#1152), and its burn is
judged clean. A strip that leans or is level refuses the welded face by
name.

Synthetic conditions only. Not exercised on a real EDM control.

Fixes #1808

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
